            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0324" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/760: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Weddell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-04-13T14:00:00-05:00">April 13, 1940—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. A secretary of the Chinese Embassy called at the Department on April 9 and
                    stated that the Chinese Government has information that the Spanish Government,
                    although it has no diplomatic representative <pb facs="0325" n="317"
                        xml:id="pg317"/> in China, is likely to recognize shortly the Wang Ching-wei
                    regime set up at Nanking on March 30. He asked whether this Government would be
                    disposed to take any action looking to dissuading the Spanish Government from
                    taking such a step. The Department desires that you take no initiative in this
                    matter but suggests that should the subject be brought up by Spanish officials,
                    you bring to the attention of those officials the attitude and position of this
                    Government as set forth in the statement to the press of March 30,<anchor n="21"
                        xml:id="d358-f1"/> quoted in Radio Bulletin No. 76.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
